why Every Horde quest of the Drowned City in one run, lead-ins included.

# The Drowned City's Horde quests in one guide: Kin'weelay's lead-in at
# Grom'gol, the pick-ups in Booty Bay and Mulgore, one run through the
# dungeon, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the guide
# picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chain: 629 The Vile Reef -> 95748 The Gurubashi Legends of Old (a
# rubbing at the Fall of Gurubashi, object 52) -> 95770 Locating the Lost City
# -> 95775 The Drowned City (four rubbings inside, items 270308-270311) ->
# 96078 A Tale Spun Around the Fire (Master Gadrin, Sen'jin Village).
# Commander Aggro'gosh's 95773 Enemies in the Water opens once 95748 is handed
# in, and his 95776 The Only Good Brinescale... (Var'Taka) follows it.
# Mazu'kon in Mulgore gives 96774 Ancient Gurubashi Idol; the idol drops from
# Deathless Marrow only for a character on the quest, so he comes before the
# run. Krazek in Booty Bay gives both factions 95789 Shady Saltseers and 95791
# The Saltseer Captain, from level 34.
#
# Inside: the data has no place inside the dungeon for its bosses, tablets or
# pearls, so those goals stand at the cave mouth (@21.4,27.9, Sunken Hollow)
# with `group 5`, and the tips lead the way. Arrival is a `goto` labelled
# "Sunken Hollow" (the area's name): done on entering the cave, or once the
# work inside is done.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: data/forever (QuestieDB Forever).
# - The way through the dungeon (the first tablet past Zul'Alai at a skull
#   totem, the second by Var'Taka in the naga wing, the third by Captain
#   Dreadrise in the pirates' plaza, the fourth by Min'loth; the Glowing Pearls
#   by Var'Taka and by Dreadrise that open the barrier to Deathless Marrow):
#   players' written accounts of their runs, November 2026 (Output Lag's
#   walkthrough).
# INGAME: the tablet spots, the pearls and the order inside come from those
# accounts only; check them on a run.

step Kin'weelay
  accept 629

step The Vile Reef
  tip The tablet lies on the sea floor among the sunken ruins west of Grom'gol. Mind your breath.
  collect 4094 quest 629.1

step Kin'weelay
  turnin 629
  accept 95748

step Fall of Gurubashi
  tip A troll ruin on the coastal hills north of the Vile Reef. Make the rubbing with the hide and charcoal, and keep them in your bags: the tablets in the Drowned City need them too.
  collect 2007 quest 95748.1

step Grom'gol Base Camp
  turnin 95748
  accept 95770
  accept 95773

step The Lost City's entrance
  tip Brinescale Skirmishers swim all over the Vile Reef, and each can drop a trident. West of the reef, a large stone tablet on the sea floor marks the mouth of an underwater cave, Sunken Hollow: swimming up to it finds the Lost City.
  collect 270305 x10 quest 95773.1
  complete 95770 @22.44,27.24

step Grom'gol Base Camp
  turnin 95770
  accept 95775
  turnin 95773
  accept 95776

step Krazek
  tip In Booty Bay. Both factions take his two quests, from level 34.
  accept 95789
  accept 95791

step Mazu'kon
  zone Mulgore
  tip Northern Mulgore. A long trip, but the idol only drops for characters on his quest.
  accept 96774

step To the Drowned City
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip A dungeon for five players of level 35 to 40. Gather your group at the cave first, as the group finder won't take you there. Dive into Sunken Hollow behind the big tablet west of the Vile Reef; the portal is inside. Water breathing helps.
  goto 21.4,27.9 "Sunken Hollow" r 25

step First tablet
  tip Up the slope past the crabs and makrura, Zul'Alai waits on a hill; he enrages near death. Past him, climb the big staircase: the first tablet stands down to your left, at the foot of a skull totem.
  collect 270308 quest 95775.1 @21.4,27.9 group 5

step Var'Taka
  tip The left wing off the central pool belongs to the naga. Var'Taka fights beside two Brinescale Priestesses who heal him; the pillars on the stairs break their line of sight. The second tablet stands beside him. Afterwards click the Glowing Pearl nearby: it is one of the two that open the barrier deeper in.
  kill 258924 quest 95776.1 @21.4,27.9 group 5
  collect 270309 quest 95775.2 @21.4,27.9 group 5

step Captain Dreadrise
  tip The right wing is the Saltseer pirates' plaza by their wrecked ship. Clear the crew before the captain: every Saltseer can drop a Voodoo-Infused Artifact, and Krazek wants three Coroners dead. The third tablet stands near Captain Dreadrise. When he is down, click the second Glowing Pearl.
  collect 270333 x10 quest 95789.1 @21.4,27.9 optional -- With several players on this quest the pirates may run out before everyone has ten: a second run finishes it.
  kill 260353 x3 quest 95791.2 @21.4,27.9 group 5
  kill 260042 quest 95791.1 @21.4,27.9 group 5
  collect 270310 quest 95775.3 @21.4,27.9 group 5

step Deathless Marrow
  tip With both pearls used, the barrier to the west is gone. Deathless Marrow waits behind it at an altar and keeps calling up adds: kill the boss, not the adds. He drops the Ancient Gurubashi Idol.
  collect 276894 quest 96774.1 @21.4,27.9 group 5

step Min'loth the Serpent
  tip Take the passage behind Deathless Marrow down the long hall. The fourth tablet stands near Min'loth, the last boss: make the rubbing before you pull him and check that it counted. At no health he turns into a serpent and heals in full.
  collect 270311 quest 95775.4 @21.4,27.9 group 5
  kill "Min'loth the Serpent" @21.4,27.9 optional group 5

step Grom'gol Base Camp
  turnin 95775
  accept 96078
  turnin 95776

step Krazek
  turnin 95791
  turnin 95789 optional -- Still short of artifacts? Krazek takes it after another run through the pirates.

step Master Gadrin
  zone Durotar
  tip Sen'jin Village, in southern Durotar.
  turnin 96078

step Mazu'kon
  zone Mulgore
  turnin 96774
